    {
      "endSeconds": 14.225,
      "index": 0,
      "sceneId": "title",
      "startSeconds": 0.25,
      "text": "Bottom line: use Agent 365 as the control plane for one accountable pilot; verify ownership, access, action traces, licenses, and preview limits before scaling."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 27.2,
      "index": 1,
      "sceneId": "control-plane",
      "startSeconds": 14.775,
      "text": "Agent 365 is the control plane for AI agents. Ask who owns each one, where it runs, what it can reach, who it affects, and what risk needs action."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 39.775,
      "index": 2,
      "sceneId": "observe-traces",
      "startSeconds": 27.75,
      "text": "Observe with a registry, activity, and health first. Add telemetry so each request, model step, tool call, and error has a trace for operators, not guesswork."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 52.275,
      "index": 3,
      "sceneId": "govern-secure",
      "startSeconds": 40.325,
      "text": "Govern and secure access as one path. Pair lifecycle review, Entra controls, Purview data checks, and Defender signals for every agent before wider rollout."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 65.5,
      "index": 4,
      "sceneId": "accountable-pilot",
      "startSeconds": 52.825,
      "text": "Keep the current agent and add only needed SDK pieces. Pilot one owned use case, verify licenses and preview limits, then scale only from evidence and review."
    }
